role      = "THE WAKING FLOOR: a vessel wakes at its MINIMUM available cap-stack and gets RAISED by recognition, never gated by absence. The unattended-reboot answer for a civic mesh, and the same law the veil-ladder runs one plane over (caps stack above a floor that never dissolves) — a THIRD occasion of the identity plane's expiring lift. GROUNDED against prior art 2026-08-08: Android Direct Boot ships it and INVERTS the vocabulary (the floor is the HARDENED state; Google now FORCES it at 72h), SPIRE + kubelet TLS bootstrap validate raise-by-recognition, Vault confirms the unfixed failure, and Tang rules that KAHU MUST NOT HOLD SHARES (a share-holder becomes the collector, colliding with bind-by-edge). Carries six named breaks — no lowering designed, a bearer-credential raise, an unsigned announcement that targets, unstamped floor reads, an unwritten shelf discipline, and 'degraded' misnaming the resting state — plus the four-way downgrade profit split where the VETO reads worst because it stays quiet"
